<!--
  The service and the permission it needs, in the same directory as the service
  itself (subplan §1.4).

  `android/` is a CNG product and is not tracked, so the usual way to say
  anything about the manifest is a config plugin — that is what
  `plugins/with-backup-rules.js` is. It has to be one because it changes
  ATTRIBUTES OF THE APPLICATION NODE, which belong to the app rather than to any
  library. This adds new ELEMENTS, and a local Expo module is a standard AGP
  library whose manifest takes part in the merge. So the declaration lives
  beside the thing it declares.

  FOREGROUND_SERVICE is not repeated here: expo-audio's plugin already puts it
  in the merged result. Criterion 16 asserts the MERGED manifest, so a line
  saved here changes nothing about what is verified.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
  <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC"/>

  <application>
    <service
      android:name=".LarkTransferService"
      android:exported="false"
      android:foregroundServiceType="dataSync"/>
  </application>
</manifest>
